   "Fujicolor PRO 160 NC Professional (Japanese-language Product Information Bulletin 163AR113A), plots on page 6 (nos. 20 特性曲線, 21 分光感度曲線, 23 色素の分光濃度曲線); the drawings are vector paths, traced end to end. Date taken from the print code イメ技・05.5-FP(HB)・2-1 next to the reference number in the footer (May 2005; no other date printed). Process printed on the plots: CN-16 (the bulletin recommends CN-16/CN-16X and also allows CN-16Q/FA/L/S and C-41). Densitometry printed as ステータスM相当 (Status M equivalent). The film is described as a high-contrast design (ハイコントラストの階調設計).",
   "Speed: daylight or electronic flash ISO 160/23 degrees; 3200 K tungsten ISO 50/18 degrees with LBB-12. No Log H Ref is printed (log_h_ref null) and no printing paper is named (print_on null; the bulletin only gives printer corrections relative to the then-current 160NC on a Color Station AF4500). Roll film base: cellulose triacetate 98 um.",
